post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
estacao-ai is installed.

Single user: run
  estacao-ai setup
It creates the data dir and its bearer token, installs and starts a user
service, wires the agents it finds (it shows the plan and asks first), and
checks the result.

System service:
  sudo systemd-sysusers /usr/lib/sysusers.d/estacao-ai.conf
  sudo systemd-tmpfiles --create /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/estacao-ai.conf
  sudo -u estacao-ai estacao-ai --data-dir /var/lib/estacao-ai --config /etc/estacao-ai/config.toml init
  sudo systemctl enable --now estacao-ai.service

Configure LLM/API keys in ~/.config/estacao-ai/env for the user service, or
/etc/estacao-ai/env for the system service. See docs/install.md for details.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat <<'EOF'
estacao-ai was upgraded.

If you use lifecycle hooks, refresh the staged hook scripts: re-run
  estacao-ai setup
(it shows the plan and asks first), or, for one agent,
  estacao-ai install-hooks --agent <name> --apply
EOF
}
